@startuml
actor Client
participant Leader
participant "Leader disk" as LD
participant Follower
participant "Follower disk" as FD
Client -> Leader : PUT / GET / DELETE [R6]
Leader -> LD : persist new entry
LD --> Leader : durable
Leader -> Follower : AppendEntries(term, prev, entries, commit)
Follower -> Follower : validate sender, term, prefix [R2,R3,R9]
Follower -> FD : persist accepted term/log/commit changes
FD --> Follower : durable
Follower --> Leader : success (matched request index)
Leader -> Leader : majority match for current-term entry [R4]
Leader -> LD : persist commit index
LD --> Leader : durable
Leader -> Leader : apply in order; capture per-entry result [R5,R6]
Leader --> Client : committed result
note over Leader,Follower
Failures/timeouts may require retry.
A timeout is an unknown outcome, not rollback.
No quorum => no new successful client operations.
end note
@enduml
